      "content": "calling it a \"classic conservative argument\" feels like you're just dismissing the point because of its politics. even if you look at it outside of a partisan lens, shouldn't justice inherently involve some level of proportional retribution to maintain social order and satisfy the moral demand for desert? if there's no punishment, is it even justice?",
